## Validation rules

A `REPORT.md` is **correctly filled** when all of the following
hold. The Phase 4 template linter verifies these mechanically.

1. All `{{...}}` placeholders are resolved.
2. `MODEL_IDENTIFIER` is the exact env-var string with no aliasing
   (DESIGN.md §2.2). Matches the run directory name.
3. §2.1 (per-field scores) is populated for every OUTPUT_SCHEMA
   field with at least the test-partition value (sacred-test-set
   first-evaluation gate). §2.2 (aggregate scores) is populated.
   §2.3 (floor compliance) is populated for every OUTPUT_SCHEMA
   field with `met` / `unmet` / `not_specified`. The Limitations
   section §7 is populated. Any of these being empty is a
   methodology failure, not a "minor formatting issue."
4. §7.1 (model lock-in caveat) is non-empty. Even "this prompt
   has not been validated on any other model" satisfies the
   constraint; an empty caveat does not.
5. §5 contains the literal block:
   ```
   Per-stage information-isolation invariants: preserved.
   - Discrepancy subagent: allow-list honored, no prior-iteration leakage.
   - Rule-edit subagent: allow-list honored, no row-content exposure.
   - Auditor subagent: allow-list honored, no score access.
   - Adversary subagent (when invoked): allow-list honored, non-persistence honored.
   ```
   The header line plus three subagent lines (discrepancy,
   rule-edit, auditor) are required unconditionally; the
   adversary line is required iff `ADVERSARY_FLAG = on` for the
   run. This is the methodology's traceable assertion that
   DESIGN.md §4.2's per-stage information-isolation design lock
   was not broken during the run. If a future runner version
   loosens any subagent's allow-list, that line cannot be
   honestly written and this validation rule fails by design.
6. `PROMPT_FROZEN_SHA256` is a 64-character lowercase hexadecimal
   string.
7. `TERMINATION_CAUSE` is one of the documented values
   (`dev-plateau`, `overfitting-guard`, `max-iterations`,
   `manual-stop`, `early-stop-floor-unmet`, `error`).
   The `early-stop-floor-unmet` value is the v0.2 EARLY_STOP
   variant introduced by `DESIGN.md` §7.1.1 per-field
   methodology application layer; when this value is set, §2.3
   floor-compliance must show at least one `unmet` row and §7.5
   acknowledged-risk overrides should name the unmet
   field(s).
8. `RECOMMENDATION` is one of the documented values (`ship`,
   `ship-with-caveats`, `do-not-ship`, `iterate-further`) and is
   followed by a non-empty rationale.
9. Confusion matrices and other per-field auxiliary structures
   in §2.1 are present in fenced code blocks per the field's
   primary metric type (confusion matrix for enum / boolean F1,
   IoU distribution for span-IoU, residual distribution for
   number-MAE / -RMSE, failure-mode breakdown for extraction
   metrics).
10. §7.5 acknowledged-risk overrides is non-empty: either a
    list of overrides (one per recorded `not-ready override` /
    `auditor override` entry in `plan.md` §11; under v0.2
    auditor overrides surface their bracketed `[edit-N.field]`
    tokens) or the literal string "None recorded." Empty
    placeholder fails this rule.
11. The §10 reproducibility checklist contains both commit hashes.
